---Eac3 Settings
---@class aws.medialive.Eac3Settings
---@field AttenuationControl? aws.medialive.Eac3AttenuationControl|string When set to attenuate3Db, applies a 3 dB attenuation to the surround channels. Only used for 3/2 coding mode.
---@field Bitrate? aws.medialive.__double Average bitrate in bits/second. Valid bitrates depend on the coding mode.
---@field BitstreamMode? aws.medialive.Eac3BitstreamMode|string Specifies the bitstream mode (bsmod) for the emitted E-AC-3 stream. See ATSC A/52-2012 (Annex E) for background on these values.
---@field CodingMode? aws.medialive.Eac3CodingMode|string Dolby Digital Plus coding mode. Determines number of channels.
---@field DcFilter? aws.medialive.Eac3DcFilter|string When set to enabled, activates a DC highpass filter for all input channels.
---@field Dialnorm? aws.medialive.__integerMin1Max31 Sets the dialnorm for the output. If blank and input audio is Dolby Digital Plus, dialnorm will be passed through.
---@field DrcLine? aws.medialive.Eac3DrcLine|string Sets the Dolby dynamic range compression profile.
---@field DrcRf? aws.medialive.Eac3DrcRf|string Sets the profile for heavy Dolby dynamic range compression, ensures that the instantaneous signal peaks do not exceed specified levels.
---@field LfeControl? aws.medialive.Eac3LfeControl|string When encoding 3/2 audio, setting to lfe enables the LFE channel
---@field LfeFilter? aws.medialive.Eac3LfeFilter|string When set to enabled, applies a 120Hz lowpass filter to the LFE channel prior to encoding. Only valid with codingMode32 coding mode.
---@field LoRoCenterMixLevel? aws.medialive.__double Left only/Right only center mix level. Only used for 3/2 coding mode.
---@field LoRoSurroundMixLevel? aws.medialive.__double Left only/Right only surround mix level. Only used for 3/2 coding mode.
---@field LtRtCenterMixLevel? aws.medialive.__double Left total/Right total center mix level. Only used for 3/2 coding mode.
---@field LtRtSurroundMixLevel? aws.medialive.__double Left total/Right total surround mix level. Only used for 3/2 coding mode.
---@field MetadataControl? aws.medialive.Eac3MetadataControl|string When set to followInput, encoder metadata will be sourced from the DD, DD+, or DolbyE decoder that supplied this audio data. If audio was not supplied from one of these streams, then the static metadata settings will be used.
---@field PassthroughControl? aws.medialive.Eac3PassthroughControl|string When set to whenPossible, input DD+ audio will be passed through if it is present on the input. This detection is dynamic over the life of the transcode. Inputs that alternate between DD+ and non-DD+ content will have a consistent DD+ output as the system alternates between passthrough and encoding.
